    {
      "id": "r20261122-a02",
      "title": "The Day the Internet Stopped",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "Last October, a damaged cable under the sea cut the internet for a whole island. For three days, nobody could send messages, watch videos, or pay with their phones. Life suddenly became very quiet.",
        "At first, people felt lost. Shops could only take cash, students could not send their homework, and nobody knew the news. But then something surprising happened: people started talking to each other. Neighbors sat outside in the evening, children played in the street, and the library was full for the first time in years.",
        "When the internet returned, many people were relieved, but some felt a little sad. The three quiet days taught them something: the internet is a wonderful tool, but it should not be the only one we have."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "damaged": "rusak",
        "cable": "kabel",
        "cut": "memutuskan",
        "cash": "uang tunai",
        "surprising": "mengejutkan",
        "neighbors": "tetangga",
        "relieved": "lega",
        "tool": "alat"
      },
      "qs": [
        {
          "q": "What caused the internet to stop?",
          "opts": [
            "A big storm",
            "A computer virus",
            "A damaged cable under the sea"
          ],
          "a": 2
        },
